A(L('3.1','Periodic Phenomena',[('3.1.A','Construct graphs of periodic relationships based on verbal representations.'),('3.1.B','Describe key characteristics of a periodic function based on a verbal representation.')],
 ['periodic relationship','period','cycle','repeating pattern','increasing','concavity','relative extremum'],
 ['Remainder of $47\\div6$?','If a pattern repeats every $4$ units, what is $f(13)$ in terms of $f$ on $[0,4)$?'],'Q1 $5$. Q2 $f(13)=f(1)$.',
 [('Period',['$f$ is periodic when its outputs repeat over successive equal-length input intervals.','The period is the smallest positive $k$ with $f(x+k)=f(x)$ for all $x$.'],
   [('One cycle of $f$ spans $-4\\le x\\le4$. What is the period?',['The cycle has length $4-(-4)=8$.','Period $=8$.']),
    ('$f$ has period $6$. Express $f(41)$ using one cycle on $[0,6)$.',['$41=6\\cdot6+5$.','$f(41)=f(5)$.'])]),
  ('Behaviour repeats every period',['Every characteristic in one period (increasing, concavity, extrema) appears in every period.','Reduce an input by whole periods to read its behaviour from one cycle.'],
   [('One cycle on $[0,4]$ increases on $(0,1)$ and decreases on $(1,4)$. On $(18,20)$?',['$18-16=2$ and $20-16=4$: the interval $(2,4)$.','Decreasing.']),
    ('Same cycle: relative max, min or neither at $x=81$?',['$81-80=1$: the maximum of the cycle.','Relative maximum at $x=81$.'])])],
 ['Period $5$: express $f(52)$ using $[0,5)$.','Cycle on $[0,6]$: concave up on $(0,3)$, concave down on $(3,6)$. Concavity on $(30,33)$?'],
 ['A Ferris wheel takes $40$ seconds per revolution. Describe a rider\'s height as a periodic relationship and give its period.','Pressure in a pump repeats every $0.8$ s. How many full cycles occur in one minute?'],
 ['Explain why the period must be the smallest positive shift that repeats the outputs.'],
 'Practice: $f(2)$; concave up. Apply: height repeats every $40$ s; $60\\div0.8=75$ cycles. Investigate: any multiple of the period also repeats the outputs, so only the smallest one describes one cycle.',
 ['Period of a pattern that repeats every $12$ units?','Period $8$: $f(70)$ equals $f$ of what on $[0,8)$?','A cycle decreases on $(2,4)$ with period $4$. On $(42,44)$?'],
 'Q1 $12$. Q2 $f(6)$. Q3 Decreasing.',
 'A periodic function repeats every period: reduce any input by whole periods and read its behaviour from one cycle.'))

